From ef41a67979aed4d7d4f393c56c1e25b6754e2b78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean Young <sean@mess.org>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 14:07:44 +0100
Subject: media: rc: After rc_unregister_device() timers can be re-armed
Git-commit: ef41a67979aed4d7d4f393c56c1e25b6754e2b78
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc1
References: git-fixes CVE-2026-99436 bsc#1291323

If rc_keydown() is called after rc_register_device(), then the timers
can be re-armed. Delete them again for a final time.

Fixes: dccc0c3ddf8f ("media: rc: fix race between unregister and urb/irq callbacks")
Signed-off-by: Sean Young <sean@mess.org>
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Acked-by: Hans Verkuil <hverkuil+cisco@kernel.org>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 drivers/media/rc/rc-main.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/rc/rc-main.c b/drivers/media/rc/rc-main.c
index ed746255b0a2..1c07bdd3b42b 100644
--- a/drivers/media/rc/rc-main.c
+++ b/drivers/media/rc/rc-main.c
@@ -1785,6 +1785,11 @@ void rc_free_device(struct rc_dev *dev)
 	if (!dev)
 		return;
 
+	if (dev->input_dev) {
+		timer_delete_sync(&dev->timer_keyup);
+		timer_delete_sync(&dev->timer_repeat);
+	}
+
 	input_put_device(dev->input_dev);
 
 	put_device(&dev->dev);
-- 
